WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.462
How can the client cut costs?

2
00:00:02.612 --> 00:00:07.731
Use it when: The client needs to cut costs, often by a target percentage.

3
00:00:07.781 --> 00:00:13.501
Ask first: Which costs are in scope, and what must not suffer (quality, safety, service)?

4
00:00:13.701 --> 00:00:16.471
Need less Stop the activity and do less of it.

5
00:00:16.521 --> 00:00:21.759
Use less per unit Cut waste and rework and get more output per person or machine.

6
00:00:21.809 --> 00:00:27.301
Pay less per unit Switch to cheaper inputs or outsource and negotiate better prices.

7
00:00:27.351 --> 00:00:34.752
Cost = how much we do × resources per unit × price per resource. Each branch cuts one factor.
